WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.030
Hello! Chilled delivery!

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.360
It's here!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.820
Your honor, please accept this!

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.920
I present sweets of brilliant gold.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:32.170
Please! Please accept this 
with my humble apologies!

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.010
When I get my next paycheck, 
I'll buy you some new games.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.890
Then we can all play together again.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.100
Okay?

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.190
I forgive you!

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.110
Yes!

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.610
Echigoya, you're quite evil yourself.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.490
<b><u>Episode 7</u></b>

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.490
Counseling for Bad Guys

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.670
I'm getting chills!

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.580
This unique texture is irresistible!

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.050
I am glad it pleases you.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.020
Indeed. I am quite satisfied.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.810
Sorry I sold your games.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.750
You should be, you jerk.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.420
I told you, I'm really sorry.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.430
Here, have some more.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.280
I shall.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.560
And while you're at it, 
would you look at this?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.180
Hey, is this...

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.980
The Nanana's Collection
 treasure from the hot springs ruins.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:16.930
Actually,Yukihime-neesan
 was at the inn, too.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.550
I think she followed us there.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.800
To get the Nanana's Collection treasure?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.600
Yeah.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.110
If she'd listened in on
 President Yuiga and the others talking,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.930
she must have known
 where the ruins were.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.040
So I had the idea to
 get the treasure before

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.190
Yukihime-neesan and her friend could.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.030
A riddle would've given me trouble,

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.770
but the ruins had a trap setup instead,

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.820
so I could make it through alone.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:45.320
And in its place, I left a
 stuffed cat I'd won at the arcade.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.820
I never thought it'd be President Yuiga to

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.250
outsmart me again, and not Yukihime-neesan.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.670
I see...

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.080
I see!

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:01.220
Wow, you really impress me, Juugo!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.790
Um...

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.300
Sorry to say it when you're 
laughing like you're truly happy,

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.550
but why are you in here?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.150
We came to have dinner.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:09.680
What?

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.640
We're having meat and potatoes today.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.260
That's not what I meant.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.550
I'm sure the door was locked.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:17.270
Look.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.190
I had a spare made in secret.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.900
You just do whatever you want, don't you?!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.370
Okay, let's eat.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.950
Here. Have some katsudon.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.410
Don't treat me like a criminal!

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.000
Sheesh...

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.840
You try to find ways to
 connect me with every single crime.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.050
That's why your deduction was off.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.270
What's this, coming from the
 man who got the jump on all of us?

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.970
Like I said, it was just a precaution

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.590
so Yukihime-neesan wouldn't steal it first...

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.670
There's no need to make excuses, Juugo.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.640
I'm actually complimenting you.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.880
I love those dirty deeds of yours!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.610
That doesn't make me happy.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.740
So, are you going to tell
 Yuiga-dono and the others about this?

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.170
Well, to be honest,

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.280
I'd rather keep it quiet
 that I'm connected to Matsuri.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:11.760
Ah, well. I lose this time.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.480
I have no intention of telling them,
 so don't worry.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.290
Still, I was surprised.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.040
By what?

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.670
I thought there was
 no way you could steal

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.170
a Nanana's Collection treasure.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.180
An early lead, stealing, lying...

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:34.890
I see all of those as essential in the 
race to obtain Nanana's Collection.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.020
You're right.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.440
But even though you
 suspected that Fugi Yukihime

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.430
would take the treasure you were after,

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:45.910
it didn't cross your mind at all that she

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.960
might steal the treasure we found.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.370
Why?

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:51.800
Who knows?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.780
It didn't cross your mind at all that she

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.030
might steal the treasure we found.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.850
<i>I just trusted her, that's all.</i>

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.510
You look gloomy.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.630
What's wrong?

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.020
N-Nothing...

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.980
I just realized that this wouldn't 
help me find out who killed you.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.580
Jeez, you don't have to make excuses.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.990
Just tell me.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.420
Actually, tell me about you.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.620
Yukihime-neesan is the 
only daughter of a family

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.440
that has supported
 Matsuri for generations.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.670
And she was my martial arts teacher.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.630
She was always strict, even as a kid...

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.800
But she'd always hold her 
hand out to me in the end.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.690
I always thought, no matter how angry

00:06:56.690 --> 00:07:00.430
she got, that part of
 her would never change.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.940
But I was wrong.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:08.000
There are unspoken
 rules in the underworld.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:12.010
Once someone has gained possession
 of something, it's off limits.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.890
That was the minimum
 respect we could show

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.660
to someone pursuing the same prey.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.760
But Yukihime-neesan tried to steal 
this without any negotiation at all.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.630
Yukihime-neesan really 
did turn her back on me.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.460
Hey, Juugo, you're crying.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.420
I am not!

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.590
You want to leave things like this?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:35.450
You haven't done anything yet.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.580
Who cares what I want!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.620
That's what she thinks of me, 
so there's nothing I can do!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.190
I'm going to ask something really basic...

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.260
Isn't it just because you 
don't like how she reacted?

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:52.230
If you don't like it,
 try to change the results.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:55.200
If that doesn't work,
 that's when you can get depressed.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.940
This isn't like you.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.000
Why did you give up from the get-go?

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:03.250
I... don't know.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.840
I get it! You want to get her attention!

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.570
Everyone wants someone
 to pay attention to them...

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.130
To notice them.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:18.010
But that goes for the other person, too.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.600
Because you know that person well,

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.320
you want to do something for them,

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:24.990
and for them to do something for you.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.640
So, when you find out that they 
don't return your feelings,

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.440
a distance forms between you.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.610
I have something I need to do.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:39.670
I'm going out.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.090
But it's late.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.290
I'm an evil guy.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.580
Just like you look.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.750
No picking on my appearance!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.960
And? What are you going to do?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.770
It's nothing important.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:57.300
I just discovered a flag in my life 
that I need to break at any cost,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.050
so I'm going to break it.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.680
I see.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.670
This is kinda scary.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:06.980
But that's all there is to it, right?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.560
If this doesn't work...

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.770
Can I cry into your chest?

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.750
Sure.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:13.990
What?! I can?!

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.800
Yeah. You can.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.080
Thank you!

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:20.200
But you don't intend to do that, do you?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.860
Oh... yeah.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.740
I know I just asked,

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:26.330
but I'm 100% sure I won't 
be crying into your chest.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.950
Well, that's too bad.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.800
I wanted to hold you close...

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.280
Uh, I'll make a correction, though.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.820
That applies to this 
particular instance only.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.850
In the future, I'll just 
be assertive and go for it!

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.350
Nope. This is a one-time-only service.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.680
Yeah, of course.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.670
Nanana-chan...

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:54.790
Uh...

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.200
Thanks.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.420
See you later!

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.330
And pick up some pudding on your way home!

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.220
Sorry to call you out here so suddenly.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.920
What do you want?

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:11.810
You wrote all that

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:15.670
nonsense about a
 "moonlight date" on the Matsuri SNS.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.130
It caused a huge stir.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:20.440
Yeah, we're a good match, aren't we?

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:23.180
You can skip that. Get to the point.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.990
Let's have a wager.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:27.810
A wager?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:31.110
If you can beat me up, I lose,

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.270
and I'll give you the
 Nanana's Collection treasure.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.880
And if you lose,

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.030
apologize to me.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.610
What did you say?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.690
Say you'll never oppose 
the young master again,

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:46.120
and kneel down and bow in apology.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:50.000
And why must I do that?

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.900
You need a reason?

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.290
Well, you can run away, if you'd prefer.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.320
I'm sure you don't want the trouble

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.380
of making up an excuse.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.140
What are the conditions for my loss?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:07.180
If I hit you even once, I win.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.220
Of course, I'll pull my punches, though.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:11.050
Hit me as hard as you can.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:14.860
No way. I'd rather die than hit a girl.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:16.670
You don't get it?

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:18.610
I'm saying you'll never hit me,

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.610
so just swing your hardest and don't worry.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:23.950
Fine.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.050
Here I come.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:49.810
Damn you!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.240
It's over, Young Master.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.390
Oh, no...

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:14.080
My power doesn't end there!

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.650
You see my power now?!

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.520
Or, more accurately,
 the power of Nanana's Collection.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:46.910
You can't escape these chains.

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:51.080
I can do whatever I want to you,

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.920
and you can't even resist as I violate you.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:59.510
By the way, you said you 
never wanted to see me again,

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.960
and you didn't care
 what happens to me, right?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.630
What of it?!

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:07.830
Then I don't care what 
happens to you, either.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.620
What... What on earth is your deal?

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:16.100
You only said things that suited you,
 then you just left home!

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:20.790
I thought you would join 
me in succeeding Matsuri.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.440
I believed that would happen,

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:27.780
but you... but you betrayed my trust!

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.450
Do as you please.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.560
Then I can come to terms with everything.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.380
I can finally hate you.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:43.620
So that's it...

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:54.320
Then I'll make it clear for you, too.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:04.850
Don't make decisions on your
 own without saying what's important,

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:06.090
Fugi Yukihime!

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:09.230
Don't do everything on your own!

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.330
I don't accept it at all!

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.410
Wh-What are you...

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.560
"What am I to you, Young Master?"

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:19.790
How am I supposed to understand 
drivel like that, you idiot?!

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.130
You should understand that 
much, you stupid child!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.750
Who could understand that?!
 It's too indirect!

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.080
You haven't had a boyfriend all your li—

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.510
I-I do have a boyfriend.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.160
Bring him here right now!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.460
I'll make that bastard regret 
touching my Yukihime-neesan!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.690
Wh-Who are you calling "yours"?!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.450
I have nothing more to say to you!

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:48.050
Well, I do!

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:52.150
I hated it! I was really depressed!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:57.120
If you betray me, who am 
I supposed to believe in?!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.150
Man, I look pathetic...

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.470
Young Master, give me a serious answer.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.430
What is Fugi Yukihime to Yama Juugo?

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.310
My first love.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.770
It was a serious answer!

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.870
What are you saying?! 
Think about where you are!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:28.300
I'll ask you one more time.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.700
Young Master, what am I to you?

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.930
Someone who will always be on my side.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:42.700
After you gave me a fake treasure?!

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.460
Y-You knew, huh?

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:48.500
I'm the one who stole the jewel.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:49.970
Of course I know that.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.910
I just didn't say anything because I knew you

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.430
must have had a reason.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.250
You believed in me that much?

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.890
It seems the same can't be said of you.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:04.520
So, after all this, you're not going 
to wriggle out of telling me, are you?

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.690
Telling you what?

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:10.570
Why you're looking for Nanana's Collection.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:16.180
Um, this is honestly a secret.

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.080
You can't tell anyone.

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:20.160
Very well.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.380
To keep a promise to a certain girl.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.500
For her sake, I need Nanana's 
Collection, whatever it takes!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.510
Y-You give me a reason like that?

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.750
And you say you hate helping people?

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.770
I meant that!

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:39.140
I honestly don't want to help anyone!

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:45.680
Really... You act all self-serving,

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.440
then you tell me to stay on your side?

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.370
Yes. That's what I am.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.650
And as such, I'm going to make 
a self-serving promise to you.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.370
I will always be on your side.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:00.950
I'll never... betray you... 
I think. Probably.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.750
Why do you sound so vague about it?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.960
Well, I can't guarantee that last part.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.390
Then what about the first part?

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:11.520
I really like you, Yukihime-neesan,

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.530
so I can promise that.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.140
You... promise?

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:19.310
Yeah. And I keep my promises.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.220
A certain older sister figure 
brought me up that way.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.240
I see.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:26.930
I don't like you that much, though.

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.960
Aw, man! I got rejected!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.290
But I suppose I'll continue to 
like you as much as I always have.

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:33.780
Really?!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.080
Only as much as I always have, understand?

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.020
Just so you know, 
unless you return to Matsuri,

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.200
I will not be on your side.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.290
That's fine.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.540
Oh, please take this.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.510
Are you sure?

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:54.520
Sure or not, it's to apologize 
for deceiving you last time.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.220
All right.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.180
And...

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.470
I need to apologize to you, too.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:07.920
When I said I had a boyfriend...

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.260
I was...

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:10.940
...lying.

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:14.400
Oh! So you really haven't 
had a boyfriend all your—

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.320
Well done.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.620
Have you been watching, Finchmatsu?

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:28.010
It's Todomatsu.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:31.380
And the older Matsuri members 
told me to come watch.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.880
You didn't post about 
this on the SNS, did you?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.450
I played it up as much as I could.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:40.590
"The young master moved on Yukihime 
and it was off into the night—"

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:45.060
You will write a post to correct that later.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.480
That's basically what happened, right?

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:49.650
You and the young master made up.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.320
And they lived happily ever after.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:53.030
There's nothing happy about it.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.540
The young master still isn't 
coming back to Matsuri.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:58.860
We don't need him, do we?

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:00.740
What did you say?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.260
Well, do we?

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:05.520
Having a guy with no motivation 
will just slow us down.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.200
Are you in any place to talk?

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.500
I am motivated.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.460
I just like cutting corners.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.620
But the young master's different.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.710
He doesn't agree with what Matsuri does.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:19.720
That issue comes before
 the issue of working together.

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.470
I do like the guy,

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.850
but frankly, I wouldn't 
want to be on his team.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.940
So that's the real Nanana's Collection 
treasure from that big house?

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.550
It seems so.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.650
And what else did you find out?

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.970
The young master seems to have a

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.140
source besides than the Adventure Club.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.080
Why do you say that?

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:45.240
He knew far too much about that 
Nanana's Collection treasure.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:49.950
I see. Should we continue 
observing him for a while, then?

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.710
No. Search for Sanada Fumika.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.860
The informer, eh?

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:57.460
You got it.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.510
<i>Yukihime-neechan!</i>

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.850
What is it, Young Master?

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.580
When we grow up,

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.290
let's work hard to help everyone 
in the world together!

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:12.500
In the world?

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:16.320
Yeah! We'll help everyone, 
and make them all happy!

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.010
All right.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.030
Then let's make a promise.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.990
Yeah! It's a promise!

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:30.440
I'm hom—

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.210
Welcome back!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:34.330
Once again... Why are you guys here?!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:41.470
Juugo, you didn't think I only 
made one spare key, did you?

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:45.560
A master detective shouldn't 
talk like a villain!

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:47.760
There, all done.

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:49.450
Thanks.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:50.490
Does it hurt?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:50.980
<i>Glory to us...</i>

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:54.350
Well, it was a pretty hard love tap.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.440
<i>And doom to the Galactic Pretty Boy!</i>

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:57.800
<i>Kiraboshi!</i>

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:00.420
Ooh, that was a very original pose!

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:02.050
Kiraboshi!

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.450
Hey, looks good!

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.640
Kiraboshi!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:08.820
I'll use that next time I bust 
up one of Juugo's schemes.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:10.250
Hey, let me join you!

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.450
<i>I'll find Nanana's Collection,</i>

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.890
Come on over.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.660
<i>and I'll find whoever killed 
Nanana-chan ten years ago.</i>

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:13.580
How do you do it?

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.930
Daruku! Go buy me that robot!

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:17.380
<i>But...</i>

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.150
<i>If Nanana-chan passes on,</i>

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.220
<i>she'll disappear from this room,
 won't she?</i>
